==Trivia==
*A ''[[wikipedia:Yandere|yandere]]'' is a type of character who is extremely obsessive in their love for another person. They will often be dangerously overprotective and possessive of the target of their love, resorting to violence to get any perceived romantic rivals out of the way. This being the theme of [[Marquis Clionius]]' debut sub-chapter could relate to portrayals of [[wikipedia:Lilith|Lilith]] as a succubus who seduces or even forces herself onto unwilling men, as Clionius' Japanese name and demonic children may reference Lilith, and its first encounter appears to have been designed for [[Lilith Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Queen Succubus Cat]], whose [[Talents]] were added in the same update as Yandere Chemistry and whose Normal Form is named Lilith Cat in [[BCEN]].
**The sub-chapter's Japanese name, Hen'ai Kagaku Jikkenjō (偏愛化学実験場, "Favoritism Chemical Test Site"), could refer to the goal of making the target show favoritism towards the obsessor.
**[[Codependent Compound]] could be a compound that makes the target codependent.
**[[Obsess-illoscope]] is a pun on ''obsess'' and ''oscilloscope''. Its Japanese name, Oshi Rosu Kōpu (推しロス・コープ, "Oshi Los Cope" or "Oshi Ross Cope"), is a pun on 推し ''oshi'' (one's favorite idol, celebrity, character, etc.) and オシロスコープ ''oshirosukōpu'' (oscilloscope), with Los/Ross Cope likely being a fictitious example of a person who is someone else's ''oshi'', and potentially either the obsessor's target or whomever the target currently gives the most attention.
**[[Envy's Flame Test]] could refer to envy towards anyone else who receives attention from the target.
**[[Smothering Scheme]] could be the obsessor's plan to make the target smother them with love, or vice versa.
**[[Distilled Devotion]]'s Japanese name, Roka Sareta Magokoro (ろ過された真心, "Filtered Sincerity" or "Filtered Devotion"), could refer to the sincere affection the target shows towards others being successfully filtered out.
**The [[Sinner Snache]]s in [[Pipette of Passion]] and Distilled Devotion may reference Lilith being associated with serpents, such as in ''[[wikipedia:Sistine Chapel ceiling#Adam and Eve|The Fall and Expulsion from Paradise]]'' on the Sistine Chapel ceiling, where the serpent in the Garden of Eden appears to be depicted as Lilith, and John Collier's painting ''[[wikipedia:Lilith (painting)|Lilith]]'', which shows a serpent coiled around her body.

